												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“We are launching Stormforge in Early access because it’s a deeply systemic, procedurally generated open world game with coop multiplayer. Community feedback will be critical to making Stormforge the best game it can be.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“Throughout Early Access, we’ll provide regular updates following our roadmap while reacting to community feedback. We currently expect to be in Early Access for approximately 1 year but it could be shorter or longer depending on community feedback. ”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“Our roadmap to 1.0 includes a new mountain biome and boss as well as new storm types, new character classes, and expanded end game content.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“At Early Access launch we’ll have 3 major biomes with unique bosses, character classes, unique storm mechanics, co-op PvE multiplayer, crafting, base building and a huge world to explore with over 100 points of interest.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“We expect to have a modest price increase for the 1.0 launch of the game, reflecting the additional content and polish added to the game. ”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We have been developing Stormforge with community feedback since the beginning and will continue to do so during Early Access and beyond. We have many ways for you to provide feedback: in-game surveys, discord feedback channels, steam discussion forums. We want to make Stormforge a great game, for you, our players. ”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
